{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Get you up from about the dwelling of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram.</b> It would have been fitting to mention On ben Pelet together with them, for so he is mentioned at the beginning of the parashah among those who entered the dispute and parted against Moses and against Aaron. But our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted that he repented and withdrew from the dispute. And thus they said in the Midrash: On ben Pelet — his wife saved him. She said to him: What difference does it make to you? If Moses is the high priest, you are a disciple; if Korah is the high priest, you are a disciple. And concerning her it is said (Proverbs 14:1): ״חכמות נשים בנתה ביתה״ — 'The wisest of women builds her house' — this is the wife of On; and ״ואולת בידיה תהרסנו״ — 'but folly tears it down with her hands' — this is the wife of Korah, who seduced him, and by her counsel he came against Moses, and she was the cause of the entire dispute, and many slain she brought down."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:10.092913717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}